title: Reformist leaders resign
new-page: true 
subtitle: Reformist disagreements with our policies have grown too severe.
tags: event
view-if: reformist_dissent >= 60
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.reformist_strength < 10) {
    Q.workers_spd -= 4; 
    Q.new_middle_spd -= 2; 
    Q.old_middle_spd -= 2; 
    Q.rural_spd -= 2; 
    Q.rb_strength -= 200; 
} else if (Q.reformist_strength < 25) {
    Q.workers_spd -= 5; 
    Q.new_middle_spd -= 3; 
    Q.old_middle_spd -= 3; 
    Q.rural_spd -= 3; 
    Q.rb_strength -= 250; 
} else if (Q.reformist_strength < 40) {
    Q.workers_spd -= 6; 
    Q.new_middle_spd -= 4; 
    Q.old_middle_spd -= 4; 
    Q.rural_spd -= 4; 
    Q.rb_strength -= 300; 
} else if (Q.reformist_strength < 60) {
    Q.workers_spd -= 8; 
    Q.new_middle_spd -= 6; 
    Q.old_middle_spd -= 6; 
    Q.rural_spd -= 6; 
    Q.rb_strength -= 350; 
} else {
    Q.workers_spd -= 10; 
    Q.new_middle_spd -= 8; 
    Q.old_middle_spd -= 8; 
    Q.rural_spd -= 8; 
    Q.rb_strength -= 400; 
}

Q.reformist_strength *= 0.3; 

Q.n_advisors_start = Q.n_advisors; 
if (Q.braun_advisor == 1) Q.n_advisors -= 1; 
if (Q.severing_advisor == 1) Q.n_advisors -= 1; 
Q.braun_advisor = 0; 
Q.severing_advisor = 0; 
Q.reformists_resign = 1; 
if (Q.n_advisors < Q.n_advisors_start) Q.shuffle_leadership_timer = 0;
!}
go-to: srpd_formed
max-visits: 1

= Reformist leaders resign

Our policy choices have greatly offended the reformist faction. Many of our most experienced leaders have resigned. 

[? if year >= 1932 : Now, many reformists have joined a splinter party, the *Sozial-Republikanische Partei Deutschlands* (Social-Republican Party of Germany), founded by former Reichsbanner leader Otto Hörsing, transforming it from a rump party into a viable competitor. They proclaim their desire to defend the Republic and the Constitution, and see us as having strayed from a pure Republican path. The SRPD has support from the workers and progressive middle class. ?]
[? if year < 1932:  Now, many reformists have formed a new splinter party, the *Sozial-Republikanische Partei Deutschlands* (Social-Republican Party of Germany), led by former Reichsbanner leader Otto Hörsing. They proclaim their desire to defend the Republic and the Constitution, and see us as having strayed from a pure Republican path. The SRPD has support from the workers and progressive middle class. ?]